decision_conditions:
Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from 9 February 2024, being the date of granting of planning permission P/2023/3637.

Reason: To prevent the accumulation of unimplemented planning permissions and to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended) and to meet the requirements of Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004 and to meet the requirements of The Town and Country Planning (Development Management Procedure) (England) Order 2015.
Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications: [Unnumbered Location Plan, Planning, Heritage, Design & Access Statement, Fire Safety Statement and Flood Risk Assessment. Received: 22/11/2023; 
01-01 Basement Floor Existing Rev D, 01- 02 Ground Floor Plan Existing Rev D, 01-03 First Floor Existing Rev D, 01-04 Second Floor Existing Rev D, 01- 05 Roof Plan Rev D, 02-01 Basement Floor Existing Rev D, 02-03 First Floor Proposed Rev D, 02-04 Second Floor Proposed Rev D, 02-05 Roof Floor Rev D, 04.4 Side Elevation (D) Rev D, 05.2 Section BB Rev D, 05.3 Section CC Rev D and 05.4 Window Detail Rev D. Received: 29/1/2024 
Cover letter and Design & Access Statement. Received: 11/05/2026;
Unnumbered Location Plan. Received: 27/07/2026;  
02-06 Ground Floor Proposed - Proposed and Approved, 04.2 FRONT ELEVATION - Proposed and Approved, 04.4 REAR ELEVATIONS - Proposed and Approved, 04.7 SIDE ELEVATION - Proposed and Approved and 05.5 Proposed and Approved Section. Received: 31/07/2026]
Reason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.
Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building, unless otherwise shown on the approved plans.
Reason: In order to safeguard the appearance of the area.
